  "id": "change-blindness",
  "term": "change blindness",
  "definition": "Change blindness is a failure to notice a visual change when it happens alongside a disruption such as an eye movement, a blink, a flash, or other distracting input. The packet also indicates that some changed visual information may still be processed implicitly even when the person cannot consciously report the change.",
